    716  fd7e							; ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    717  fd7e							; VCS3 — OvShutScan body (Phase C kill test; bank2 tramp `sta $1FF9 / jmp
    718  fd7e							; $FD80` at $FE48). IN: A = kill clock (EnemyRamP-1), Y = MetaB b6 hot bit
    719  fd7e							; ($40/0 — staged bank2-side; MetaB lives in bank2 models_data ROM, a
    720  fd7e							; (RoomPF0Lo),Y fetch here would see bank3's pad). OUT (2026-10-14b):
    721  fd7e							; C=0 passable (A ignored) / C=1 + A≠0 kill / C=1 + A=0 SOLID block —
    722  fd7e							; returned through the $FBEE pad (sta $1FF8 executed here, rts fetched
    723  fd7e							; from bank2's byte-identical copy) to OvShutBand's jsr — A and C
    724  fd7e							; survive both; X/Y clobbered (OvShutBand reloads A before the latch).
    725  fd7e							; Kill semantics (user spec 2026-10-14, superseded the 2026-10-13
    726  fd7e							; endpoint-only rule): a horizontal containment gate (after the clock
    727  fd7e							; math, before the hot/cold split) — the player's lit span must sit
    728  fd7e							; inside the column [BallX-7, BallX] or the call returns passable
    729  fd7e							; (side brush, user bug 2026-10-14: touching the closed block from the
    730  fd7e							; side is not a crunch). Then hot band (MetaB b6) = touching ANY
    731  fd7e							; closed slice kills (endpoint test ≡ any-part: the ping-pong states
    732  fd7e							; $11/$1B/$1F never have a closed middle with open ends). Cold band =
    733  fd7e							; containment only: kill iff the whole sprite sits inside CLOSED
    734  fd7e							; slices (crunched) — $1F trivially; $1B/$11 iff the box misses the
    735  fd7e							; aperture (H≥gapHi or F<gapLo). Touching an edge from the open side
    736  fd7e							; is not a cold kill — that is what the hot flag is for. Every
    737  fd7e							; NON-kill outcome (side brush, opening half, totally closed, the
    738  fd7e							; aperture at the player's Y) goes through the solidity test
    739  fd7e							; (.V3solidBody): both endpoints open → passable, else SOLID block —
    740  fd7e							; the punched cell must not be walkable through a closed shutter
    741  fd7e							; (user 2026-10-14b).
    742  fd7e							; Clock parity: RefreshEnemyY inc'd EnemyRamP at overscan entry, so
    743  fd7e							; clock-1 = the exact value the kernel rendered slices from this frame.
    744  fd7e							; Endpoints: RoomY (head) + RoomY+11 (feet = PLAYER_SPRITE_H-1) — every
    745  fd7e							; open state's gap is >=13 lines ($1B = the 13-line center slice), so
    746  fd7e							; both endpoints open ⟺ the whole sprite is clear of that state.
    747  fd7e							; Ping-pong constants (#32/#4) = bank2 VcrCoveredState + CrunchClock
    748  fd7e							; (verify_build check_crunch_clock asserts the trio).
